# The staged set the release workflow made with `mopm stage` (docs/ci.md, "The mopm
# jobs"), as a build input: every file of this directory but this one. The job
# `mopm-stage` of .github/workflows/release.yml writes it here (`mopm stage --out
# release/staged_set`: plan.json, `<subdir>/<file>.conda`, `<name>/README.md`) and then
# builds //release/readme_e2e/verify:all with `-c komira_release.staged=stage`, which
# installs from this target. The files are not in the repository (.gitignore), so the
# target is empty in a checkout, and the e2e against it fails on the missing plan.json:
# a release that did not stage fails.
#
# `mopm stage` asks the registry which versions it already holds, so it cannot run as a
# build action (an action is offline): the farm gets the set it wrote as an input, and
# the README e2e runs on the farm against those bytes.
filegroup(
    name = "set",
    srcs = glob(["**"], exclude = ["BUCK"]),
    visibility = ["//release/readme_e2e/verify:"],
)
